= Shichang (Ray) Zhang
# Toward a holistic scientific understanding of trustworthy AI

~~~
{}{img_left}{img/bio2.jpg}{Photo of Shichang Zhang}{280}{320}{https://shichangzh.github.io/}

== About Me
I am Shichang (Ray) Zhang, an Assistant Professor in the [https://wpcarey.asu.edu/information-systems-degrees Department of Information Systems] at the W. P. Carey School of Business, Arizona State University. Before joining ASU, I was a postdoctoral fellow at the [https://d3.harvard.edu/ Harvard Business School AI Institute] working with [https://himalakkaraju.github.io/ Hima Lakkaraju]. I received my Ph.D. in [https://www.cs.ucla.edu/ Computer Science at UCLA], advised by [http://web.cs.ucla.edu/~yzsun/ Yizhou Sun]. I received my M.S. in [https://statistics.stanford.edu/ Statistics at Stanford] and my B.A. in [https://statistics.berkeley.edu/ Statistics at Berkeley]. My research aims to *scientifically understand AI to ensure it is trustworthy and beneficial to humanity*. I have developed principled methods to analyze and improve the trustworthiness of AI systems, from model mechanisms to training processes to data features. 

# (1) Model-wise, I study large language models (LLMs) to reveal their [https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.02904 internal mechanisms] and [https://arxiv.org/pdf/2307.10635v2 reasoning capabilities], enabling task-specific [https://arxiv.org/pdf/2406.09612 interpretable models] built on them. (2) Training-wise,  I develop techniques to measure the training influence on AI behavior, providing new tools for [https://openreview.net/pdf?id=ghp4GWDFd1 training data assessment], [https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.00175 model auditing, and credit assignment to developers]. (3) Data-wise, I design methods to [https://arxiv.org/pdf/2201.12380 examine how data features drive AI decisions], allowing non-expert users to interpret and effectively use AI in [https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/abs/10.1287/isre.2023.0029?journalCode=isre healthcare], [https://arxiv.org/pdf/2401.08627 science], and [https://arxiv.org/pdf/2302.12465 e-commerce] applications. 
# Collectively, my research moves beyond black-box empiricism toward a holistic scientific understanding for trustworthy AI

